[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3385430422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3385430422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3385430422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JyZGW","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T11:30:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T11:30:12Z","body":"Does it help if you increase the max domain a little beyond 1.0 (like 1.01 or even 1.1), and specify the end point to that limit?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3385430422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3396944315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3396944315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3396944315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KeUG7","user":{"login":"vreedw","id":236834535,"node_id":"U_kgDODh3O5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236834535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw","html_url":"https://github.com/vreedw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T10:46:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-13T10:46:48Z","body":"> Does it help if you increase the max domain a little beyond 1.0 (like 1.01 or even 1.1), and specify the end point to that limit?\n\nNo, I think WidthTexture only records info from 0.0 to 1.0. Increasing domain seems to only decrease accuracy, which is a separate issue. After skimming the source code, I think the original issue is just a case of recording in 'for < width' loop instead of 'for <= width' ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3396944315/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3415314126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3415314126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3415314126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LkY7O","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T12:15:04Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T12:15:04Z","body":"It seems that the result `texture()` isnot as expected.\n﻿\n- It returns `width=0.0` when `UV.y==0.00784`\n- It returns `width=0.00784` when `UV.y==0.02553`\n﻿\n\nI am curious if there are some kind of sampling algorithm to generate textures that are consistent with the OpenGL algorithm?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3415314126/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418650010","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3418650010","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3418650010,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LxHWa","user":{"login":"vreedw","id":236834535,"node_id":"U_kgDODh3O5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236834535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw","html_url":"https://github.com/vreedw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-18T16:49:24Z","updated_at":"2025-10-18T16:50:24Z","body":"If you're talking about variable width inside the shader, then it should not correlate with UV.y. It correlates to _curve point height_ or _CurveTexture pixel brightness_. For example if curve is f(x) = 0.4, then width is always 0.4 no matter the UV.y. \n\n>     * It returns `width=0.0` when `UV.y==0.00784`\nAt `UV.y==0.00784` it should sample brightness of the very first pixel, which is 0.0, as expected.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418650010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419133134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3419133134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3419133134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ly9TO","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-19T01:53:50Z","updated_at":"2025-10-19T01:53:50Z","body":"@vreedw \n\nI don't know much about shaders. Here are my testing steps.\n\n1. Create a smallest `CurveTexture` with width=32.\n2. Modify screen size to 32x32\n3. Modify shader to `COLOR = vec4(UV.y)`, capture the screen using RenderDoc. (But I got a 64x64 image), Fetch the first point's color is (0.00784, 0.00784, 0.00784, 1), expected (0, 0, 0, 1). BTW UV.x and UV.y have same result.\n4. Modify shader to `COLOR = vec4(width)`, capture the screen using RenderDoc. (64x64 again), Fetch the first point's color is (0, 0, 0, 1), as expected.\n\nMy environment is ubuntu 24.04, compilatible rendering mode.  I also print the curve data's 32 points, they are as expected.\n\nSo I guess there are some sampling algorithm which making different between curve data created image and `texture()` result in shader. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419133134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3502135859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3502135859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3502135859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Qvloz","user":{"login":"vreedw","id":236834535,"node_id":"U_kgDODh3O5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236834535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw","html_url":"https://github.com/vreedw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vreedw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T11:55:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T11:55:18Z","body":"@rsubtil\nFound the actual issue and tested the fix by recompiling the engine. I would be very thankful if bug fixing process could be expedited.\n\nThe problem was this line 102: `float t = i / static_cast<float>(_width);`\nSince iterator i was from this loop `for (int i = 0; i < _width; ++i)`, the problematic line would end at **t = width-1 / width**, which was the cause of the last missing pixel. The fixed line would then be `float t = i / static_cast<float>(_width-1);`\n\nWhile at it I also fixed the issue of CurveTexture always assuming domain is [0.0, 1.0] as I mentioned earlier. The issue was at the same line, and the fix would look like this: `float t = curve.get_min_domain() + i / static_cast<float>(_width - 1) * (curve.get_max_domain() - curve.get_min_domain());`.\n\nThe same fix should be applied 3 more times for each color in CurveTextureXYZ section in the same file without forgetting to change name of the curve variable for each.\n\nWith these fixes and removal of the float_offset provided in shader of MRP, one could see that line would go from the center of top left pixel to the center of bottom right pixel with both edge anchor points being recorded, showing that CurveTexture works as intended with any domain.\n\nP.S. While looking for the problem I stumbled upon this line 511 `for (int i = 1; i < _bake_resolution - 1; ++i) {`  in curve.cpp. For _bake_resolution = 4, It would run only i = 1 and i = 2, which I believe was not the intention.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3502135859/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506590775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111413#issuecomment-3506590775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413","id":3506590775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RAlQ3","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-08T14:18:45Z","updated_at":"2025-11-08T14:18:45Z","body":"Thanks for your analysis @vreedw! If you're up for it, go ahead and open a PR with your changes, as that is the best way to get more visibility and feedback by engine contributors.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506590775/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]